1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,520
Heat with oil and own a heat pump? One evaluation's advice: switch
the heat pump off on the coldest days and let the oil burner run.

2
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:21,537
The switch-off point was 8 degrees Fahrenheit in 2015 and 25 the year after, set by that year's
oil and electricity prices and the heat pump's cold performance; dearer oil moves it lower.

3
00:00:22,567 --> 00:00:33,223
That is one evaluation of ductless mini-splits, and the advice is for oil-heated
homes only: against propane and electric resistance it found the heat pump cheaper.

4
00:00:34,233 --> 00:00:41,601
If you heat with oil, ask which heater runs cheaper at this year's
prices; the full inquiry asks where a heat pump pays at all.
